WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.300
Before you speak: the three elements of presentation style.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:09.170
Tika knows her material. But she walks in looking at the floor, and her hands will not stay still.

3
00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:15.950
The audience reads your body before it hears your words. If the two disagree, the body wins.

4
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:23.400
Presentation style has three elements. Physical presence: what they see. Vocal emphasis: what they hear under the words. And emotional connection: what they feel when you read the room and respond.

5
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.700
Presence is prepared, not performed. Before she walks in next time, Tika does three things. Feet flat on the floor. Three slow breaths, longer out than in. And a home for her hands.

6
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:40.060
The same elements change with the room. One to one: stillness, eye contact, a slower pace. A small meeting: sit forward. A large room: wider gestures and real pauses. A video call: look at the lens and add energy.

7
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:46.050
The next presentation has the same material. This time her body says what her words say.

8
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:52.650
She did not copy anyone. She adjusted the elements, not her personality.

9
00:00:53.050 --> 00:01:00.050
The body speaks first. Presence is prepared, not performed.

10
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:04.850
Now it is your turn. Before your next meeting: feet, three breaths, a home for your hands.
